course: dictionary
lesson: 12550
title: Detonate: a word about explosions
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To detonate means to set off a bomb or explosive on purpose, or to explode suddenly with a loud bang. «The bomb squad detonated the old bomb from a safe distance.» The word tells you the blast was made to happen. Nobody dropped it by accident.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The fireworks detonated high in the sky with a loud bang.» The bang is a clue that something exploded suddenly, so detonate must mean to explode with a loud noise.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "set off on purpose" for detonated in the first sentence. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Detonate is a verb, so it changes: detonates, detonated, detonating.
fact: Detonate is a verb, which means an action word.
fact: «Detonate» means to make a bomb or explosive go off on purpose.
fact: «Detonate» can also mean to explode suddenly with a loud bang.
fact: A «controlled explosion» is planned carefully so that it is safe, for example when a bomb squad makes an old bomb safe.
fact: The forms are detonate, detonates, detonated and detonating. «Detonated» tells you it happened in the past.
exercise: «The bomb squad detonated the old bomb from a safe distance.» What does detonated mean? | Put away carefully in a box | Painted bright red | Dropped by accident | *Set off on purpose
exercise: Find and copy the word from «The fireworks detonated high in the sky with a loud bang.» that means a sudden loud noise. | sky | high | fireworks | *bang
exercise: Which phrase means a planned explosion that is made safe? | A quiet walk in the park | *A controlled explosion | A gentle breeze | A sleepy yawn
test: «The engineer will detonate the charge at noon.» What does detonate mean? | To sleep quietly | *To set off on purpose | To make a sandwich | To paint a wall
test: Which word is the past tense of detonate? | *detonated | detonating | detonates | detonate
exam: Which sentence uses detonate correctly, meaning to explode with a loud bang? | *The firework detonated with a loud bang over the town | The dog detonated its bone under the table | The baker detonated the cake for the party | The kettle detonated the tea
